url.parse: "example.com/x" isn't a URL: it has no scheme, like https:, at the start; for a URL relative to another, use url.join(base, ref)
url.parse: "/just/a/path" isn't a URL: it has no scheme, like https:, at the start; for a URL relative to another, use url.join(base, ref)
url.parse: "http://" isn't a URL: it has no host; write one after http://
url.parse: "http://a:99999/" isn't a URL: the port is past 65535
url.parse: "http://a:8x/" isn't a URL: the port must be a number, not "8x"
url.parse: "http://[1::2::3]/" isn't a URL: "[1::2::3]" isn't an IPv6 address
url.parse: "http://[1:2:3:4:5:6:7:8:9]/" isn't a URL: "[1:2:3:4:5:6:7:8:9]" isn't an IPv6 address
url.parse: "http://[::1/" isn't a URL: "[::1" isn't an IPv6 address
url.parse: "http://exa mple.com/" isn't a URL: a host can't hold ' '
url.parse: "http://a%20b/" isn't a URL: a host can't hold ' '
url.parse: "http://a<b/" isn't a URL: a host can't hold '<'
url.parse: "http://1.2.3.256/" isn't a URL: the host ends in a number but isn't an IPv4 address
url.parse: "http://1.2.3.4.5/" isn't a URL: the host ends in a number but isn't an IPv4 address
url.parse: "http://user@/x" isn't a URL: it has no host; write one after http://
url.parse: "http://:80/" isn't a URL: it has no host; write one after http://
url.parse: "file://user@host/x" isn't a URL: a file: URL can't have a user name, password or port
url.parse: "file://host:21/x" isn't a URL: a file: URL can't have a user name, password or port
url.parse: "foo://a b/" isn't a URL: a host can't hold the character 0x20
url.build: the parts need a scheme, like {"scheme": "https", ...}
url.build: "hostname" isn't a part of a URL; the parts are scheme, username, password, host, port, path, query and fragment
url.join: "mailto:a@b" can't have a relative URL resolved against it, only a #fragment
